turtles\"\n    (small values at the end of the list) by using a gap larger than 1 for\n    comparisons, which progressively shrinks by a factor (commonly 1.3).\n    Once the gap reaches 1, the algorithm effectively becomes Bubble Sort\n    for the final passes, but typically with fewer overall comparisons and swaps\n    due to earlier passes moving elements more drastically.\n\n    Args:\n        data: The list of comparable elements to be sorted (e.g., integers, floats).\n              The elements must support comparison operators (`>`, `<`).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the sorted elements in ascending order.\n        The original input list remains unchanged.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> comb_sort([5, 15, 37, 25, 79])\n        [5, 15, 25, 37, 79]\n    \"\"\"\n    arr = list(data)  # Create a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the new gap\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False # Reset swapped flag for the current pass\n\n        # Perform a \"bubble sort\" pass with the current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n    \n    return arr", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/74": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(sequence: list, patterns: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given sequence list follows a specified patterns list based on\n    a strict one-to-one mapping rule.\n\n    This function checks for a bi-directional one-to-one mapping between elements\n    of `sequence` and `patterns`. Each unique element in `sequence` must map to\n    exactly one unique element in