cifiers\n                   (e.g., passing a string to '{0:d}').\n        ValueError: If a value error occurs during string formatting, typically\n                    due to invalid format specifiers or missing arguments required\n                    by the format string that cannot be resolved from the single\n                    `element` argument.\n        AttributeError: If `format_string` is not a string and therefore lacks\n                        a `.format()` method.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Adhering to the design's algorithm: iterate, apply format, collect results.\n    # A list comprehension provides a concise and efficient way to achieve this.\n    # The `format_string.format(element)` call strictly follows the\n    # specification in the SRS and Design Document.\n    return [format_string.format(element) for element in input_list]", "base_status": "fail", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/394": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/394", "solution": "def check_distinct(data_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if all elements within a given tuple are unique (i.e., contain no duplicates).\n\n    Args:\n        data_tuple: The tuple to be checked for distinct elements. Elements within the tuple\n                    must be hashable.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if all elements in data_tuple are distinct, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return len(data_tuple) == len(set(data_tuple))", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "Mbpp/395": [{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "from collections import Counter\nfrom typing import Optional\ndef first_non_repeating_character(s: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeating character in a given string.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string (can be empty).\n\n    Returns:\n        The first non-repeating character as a string, or None if no such character exists\n        or the input string is empty.\n